{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"e11c3bef-3b37-47fe-a078-3380a15cf81d","agentId":"a0b3aefd808268adb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are a skeptical, READ-ONLY code reviewer (write nothing: no files, no git changes, do not open the Orca GUI window; ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 node-mode runs are fine; never kill processes you did not start, never kill by pattern). Review `git -C /home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles/.drovr/wt/orca-cli-skills diff origin/master..HEAD` (orca.nix, tests/orca-cli-skills.sh, tests/sandbox-fonts.sh). Angles: correctness and error-handling. Round 8; `git log origin/master..HEAD` records each round's fixes and the limitations deliberately accepted and documented (the startup race before bwrap forks; traps set after `&`; a targeted `kill -INT` to a launcher in a terminal's foreground is lost; a group-wide HUP/TERM reaching the packaged GUI twice is abrupt) — do not re-raise those unless you can show a cheap fix or that they are worse than documented.\n\nNewest change (d892f61a): `fwd` now loops (≤100 × 0.05s) while bwrap's child still has the signal in SigIgn, reading /proc/$child/task/$child/children with `read` (no trailing newline) and the child's /proc/<pid>/status; tests start payloads under `set -m` instead of setsid. Scrutinize: correctness of that loop (pid changes as layers exec? — exec keeps the pid; container-init's ldconfig child; kid that exits mid-loop; a trap running a 5s loop while another signal arrives — nested traps in bash; the main `wait` loop's interaction); does `kill -l \"$1\"` give the right number for HUP/INT/TERM; does the INT foreground check still work; test validity under `set -m` with and without a tty, and in CI (.forgejo/workflows/nix-eval.yml tool shell: bash coreutils grep sed gawk git jq diffutils — check every command the test uses is in it). Built outputs via `nix eval --raw .#homeConfigurations.shiori.config.home.packages --apply ...` in the worktree.\n\nRate every finding Critical / Important / nit with file:line; say explicitly when none at a severity. Final message = findings."},"uuid":"16a15100-27d0-4d1e-90cf-1af97c25e7b5","timestamp":"2026-10-24T12:29:20.428Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/sauyon/devel/dotfiles/.drovr/wt/orca-cli-skills","sessionId":"d19ff9ff-38c8-4378-ac54-4f4061f74300","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"orca-cli-skills"}
